    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d139">

                <pb facs="0194" n="1028" xml:id="pg1028"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112A/1823a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-05-08T15:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 8, 1918, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Government considering possibility of establishment of white list for China and
                    has cabled instructions for consuls to report on names appearing on British list
                    and such eliminations from and additions thereto as they have to suggest. Whole
                    question of cooperation in war trade policies under discussion here with
                    Japanese Ambassador.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
